<section id="gmat-quant" class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>What's on the GMAT Quant section</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">The current GMAT (Focus Edition) has three 45-minute sections — Quantitative Reasoning, Verbal Reasoning and Data Insights — 64 questions in total, taken in any order you choose.</p>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Format</h3>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>21 Problem Solving questions (multiple choice)</li>
          <li>45 minutes — about 2 minutes 8 seconds each</li>
          <li>Computer-adaptive: difficulty adjusts to your answers</li>
          <li>No calculator allowed</li>
          <li>You can review and change up to 3 answers per section</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Content tested</h3>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li><strong>Arithmetic:</strong> number properties, fractions, percents, ratios</li>
          <li><strong>Algebra:</strong> equations, inequalities, functions, exponents</li>
          <li><strong>Word problems:</strong> rates, work, mixtures, interest</li>
          <li><strong>Statistics &amp; counting:</strong> averages, sets, probability, combinatorics</li>
          <li>Plane geometry was removed; Data Sufficiency moved to Data Insights</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Scoring</h3>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>Quant section score: 60–90</li>
          <li>Total GMAT score: 205–805</li>
          <li>All three sections weigh equally in your total</li>
          <li>Unanswered questions cost you — pacing is a real skill</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><span>1</span><h3>Create a free account</h3><p>Takes one minute. Tell us your test date and target score.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><span>2</span><h3>Free 1-on-1 Zoom session</h3><p>We work a few timed questions together, spot your weak areas, and build a study plan.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><span>3</span><h3>Join the bootcamp</h3><p>Four weeks of live classes, practice sets and direct support until test day.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="bootcamp" class="section">
  <div class="wrap bootcamp">
